        "id": "AML.T0020",
        "name": "Training Data Poisoning",
        "description": "Adversaries may manipulate data used for training or fine-tuning an AI model to influence the resulting model's behavior. Adversaries may add, remove, or modify data samples; alter labels or annotations; or manipulate feedback and data-collection processes.\n\nTraining data poisoning may cause targeted errors, introduce biased or unsafe behavior, degrade model performance, or embed backdoors activated by specific inputs. The resulting behavior may persist in the trained model after the poisoned data is no longer accessible.\n\nAdversaries may poison data directly after gaining access to a training pipeline, or poisoned datasets may be introduced through [AI Supply Chain Compromise](/techniques/AML.T0010).",
        "tacticId": "AML.TA0006",
        "tacticName": "Persistence",
