        "id": "AML.T0109",
        "name": "AI Supply Chain Rug Pull",
        "description": "Adversaries may publish legitimate AI components or software, gain user adoption, then push an update with a malicious variant, leading to [AI Supply Chain Compromise](/techniques/AML.T0010). More scrutiny is often placed on a supply chain dependency when it is first being considered for inclusion in an AI system. Performing a rug pull may allow adversaries to bypass these defenses and be more likely to achieve [Initial Access](/tactics/AML.TA0004).\n\nAdversaries may [Publish Poisoned AI Artifacts](/techniques/AML.T0115), then attempt to gain user trust and increase adoption before performing the rug pull (See [AI Supply Chain Reputation Inflation](/techniques/AML.T0111)).",
        "tacticId": "AML.TA0007",
        "tacticName": "Defense Evasion",
        "tactics": [
          {
            "id": "AML.TA0007",
            "name": "Defense Evasion"
          }
        ],
        "isSubtechnique": false,
